WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Suppose a developer searches stripe 401 invalid API key,

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.867
and two docs pages answer it.

3
00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:09.547
That's where docs SEO starts,

4
00:00:09.547 --> 00:00:11.967
because one page should own each task,

5
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:13.733
so I'd fold the other into it.

6
00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:16.893
A crawler then has to reach it through a plain link,

7
00:00:16.893 --> 00:00:19.413
and I'd read the source HTML,

8
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:23.433
because a browser can make a broken page look healthy.

9
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:24.893
Then its canonical tag,

10
00:00:24.893 --> 00:00:27.873
sitemap and links should name one URL,

11
00:00:27.873 --> 00:00:32.453
because disagreement usually means parts of the site prefer different URLs.

12
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:35.053
So I'd save a baseline first,

13
00:00:35.053 --> 00:00:37.473
then fix each blocking failure in that order,

14
00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:39.793
so I can explain what moved.
